  "worked_solution": "First, let's round the number of babies born in the New York Hospital to the nearest $10$:\n\n- Boys: $102⟶100$\n\n- Girls: $81⟶80$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the number of boys to the number of girls (expressed as a fraction) is approximately:\n\n$$\n\\frac{100}{80}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the number of boys and the denominator represents the number of girls.\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $10$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{100÷10}{80÷10}=\\frac{10}{8}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{10÷2}{8÷2}=\\frac{5}{4}\n$$\n\nWe can make a denominator of $120$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $30$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\times 30}{4\\times 30}=\\frac{150}{120}\n$$\n\nTherefore, approximately $150$ boys were born at Boston Hospital in that particular month.",
